WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.263
GRADE 2 CLASS 2

00:14.014 --> 00:15.515
Wow. Wow.

00:15.598 --> 00:17.100
What a turn of events...

00:17.183 --> 00:18.184
IN SUSPENSE
BA-DUMP BA-DUMP

00:18.268 --> 00:21.438
How in the world did they adapt this plot
twist for the screen?

00:22.188 --> 00:25.233
Another movie based on their books will
be streaming this week.

00:25.316 --> 00:28.486
I saw that film back when I was in
junior high.

00:29.362 --> 00:30.196
With Igarashi.

00:31.364 --> 00:32.699
I really enjoyed it.

00:33.241 --> 00:36.119
Didn't get it.
They completely lost me halfway through.

00:37.912 --> 00:38.747
Wait...

00:38.830 --> 00:41.332
I thought that movie was really
entertaining. but...

00:42.959 --> 00:44.502
Maybe I'm the only one?

00:45.962 --> 00:46.921
What should I do?

00:47.797 --> 00:50.008
I want Amamiya to read the original work.

00:50.091 --> 00:51.551
FULL OF ONESELF

00:53.803 --> 00:54.637
PEEK

00:54.721 --> 00:57.432
- GRADE 2 CLASS 3
- Hey, Amamiya.

00:57.515 --> 00:58.975
You scared me!

00:59.059 --> 01:00.769
What's going on?

01:00.852 --> 01:01.686
Um.

01:04.397 --> 01:06.524
The film we were talking about
this morning...

01:06.608 --> 01:10.445
I have the book that it was based on, so...

01:12.072 --> 01:14.741
If you want, you're free to borrow it.

01:15.825 --> 01:19.329
MUTTER MUTTER MUMBLE MUMBLE

01:19.412 --> 01:22.957
Well, um, I figured reading the
book might give the movie more context.

01:23.041 --> 01:24.375
I'll read it! I'd love to!

01:25.168 --> 01:26.002
Hm?

01:28.171 --> 01:29.005
Wow...

01:30.715 --> 01:32.467
That'd make me super happy.

01:36.888 --> 01:37.722
Huh?

01:38.681 --> 01:40.683
Oh, thank goodness!

01:41.559 --> 01:42.393
FLOOF FLOOF

01:44.229 --> 01:45.063
Thank you.

01:47.524 --> 01:50.110
At first, I didn't peg him as the kind of
guy that...

01:50.819 --> 01:52.153
How should I put it?

01:54.614 --> 01:57.325
HEEHEE...

01:57.408 --> 01:58.785
- What's up?
- He's adorable.

02:10.130 --> 02:12.006
STRETCH, SWISH

02:12.090 --> 02:14.717
I got carried away and recommended
it to him, but I hope he didn't feel

02:14.801 --> 02:15.635
pressured.

02:16.136 --> 02:17.470
I'll read it. I'd love to!

02:18.221 --> 02:20.807
Wow. That'd make me super happy.

02:38.825 --> 02:39.784
- Good morning.
- Ah...

02:39.868 --> 02:40.702
Morning!

02:41.953 --> 02:43.413
You're heading out already?

02:43.496 --> 02:44.414
Yeah.

02:44.497 --> 02:46.416
I have to prepare for a meeting today.

02:46.916 --> 02:47.750
Oh, okay.

02:47.834 --> 02:50.295
I left money.
It's right next to the whiteboard.

02:50.378 --> 02:51.629
Oh, thanks.

02:51.713 --> 02:53.131
Lock the door. okay.

02:53.214 --> 02:54.174
Well, I'm off.

02:55.008 --> 02:55.842
Have a good day.

03:03.308 --> 03:05.602
Mom always leaves for work early.

03:06.769 --> 03:08.313
MONEY FOR MEALS

03:08.396 --> 03:11.649
And since the divorce, she's started
coming home later and later.

03:13.067 --> 03:15.403
And when I'm at home, I'm almost
always alone.

03:19.157 --> 03:23.411
Sometimes I wonder if I even exist
to them.

03:24.662 --> 03:27.624
No, no.
It's different for our household, though.

03:28.458 --> 03:29.292
I guess...

03:32.712 --> 03:35.590
For me, anyway, it's business as usual.

05:01.342 --> 05:03.678
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

05:07.640 --> 05:12.020
Thunder

05:12.854 --> 05:14.939
What? Really? No way.

05:15.690 --> 05:18.067
Okay, tell me.
How did you find your part-time job?

05:18.151 --> 05:21.446
There weren't any good ones in the
free newspaper when I looked.

05:21.529 --> 05:23.239
Uh... Um...

05:23.323 --> 05:26.909
I even signed up on this app and have
been searching everywhere, but-

05:26.993 --> 05:29.412
But why? Why all of a sudden? Uh!

05:33.583 --> 05:35.835
STARE

05:35.918 --> 05:36.753
Hm.

05:39.088 --> 05:40.840
SMILE

05:42.675 --> 05:43.926
Her beauty's blinding me.

05:45.511 --> 05:46.346
Weird.

05:46.429 --> 05:49.557
Koyun's suddenly being real friendly with
a first-year.

05:49.640 --> 05:50.516
What's happening?

05:51.017 --> 05:52.477
Yeah. What's going on?

05:53.061 --> 05:53.895
So weird.

05:53.978 --> 05:54.812
REPLAY SMILE

05:57.065 --> 05:58.649
Not to mention, she's so pretty!

05:58.733 --> 05:59.609
What's she up to?

06:01.527 --> 06:02.904
Didn't see that coming.

06:03.988 --> 06:05.239
Okay, break's over.

06:05.323 --> 06:06.908
First-years, come circle up.

06:09.202 --> 06:10.036
Oh.

06:10.119 --> 06:12.330
Sounds like the upperclassmen are calling
me.

06:12.413 --> 06:13.456
Okay.

06:13.539 --> 06:16.751
WAVE WAVE

06:23.508 --> 06:25.426
TAP TAP TAP, THUMP THUMP, WHACK

06:25.510 --> 06:26.344
Okay.

06:29.931 --> 06:30.807
Uh. Mm.

06:33.601 --> 06:35.728
Jeez. Stop, Hayat-

06:40.191 --> 06:41.025
Ugh.

06:43.194 --> 06:44.654
Sorry. Did I surprise you?

06:44.737 --> 06:45.863
PAYBACK FOR THE OTHER DAY

06:45.947 --> 06:49.200
- Uh-huh.
- I can't see Miki and Tsukiko anywhere.

06:49.700 --> 06:51.953
Oh. So she's just gonna sit here.

06:56.416 --> 06:57.250
Minato.

06:58.584 --> 06:59.460
What was that?

06:59.961 --> 07:01.462
Anyway, about the tournament...

07:01.963 --> 07:05.675
We're short on controllers, so could you
bring yours from home Sunday?

07:06.259 --> 07:08.594
- Video games, huh...
- How many people are coming?

07:08.678 --> 07:10.513
- Just us three.
- Oh, man, you know what I wish we had?

07:10.596 --> 07:12.098
A racing wheel. That'd be sick.

07:12.181 --> 07:13.641
Just buy one, Hayato.

07:13.724 --> 07:15.226
Wait. Why do I have to buy it?

07:17.728 --> 07:18.896
FWUMP

07:19.397 --> 07:20.523
DÉJÀ VU

07:20.606 --> 07:23.651
But I've gotta be in the way right now,
aren't I?

07:24.277 --> 07:25.611
Uh. No.

07:25.695 --> 07:26.529
Sorry.

07:27.196 --> 07:30.074
I could care less whether you're in
the way or not.

07:33.119 --> 07:35.163
I just want you to be here.

07:38.249 --> 07:39.667
That's- That's all it is...

07:40.960 --> 07:41.794
For me.

07:43.713 --> 07:44.547
Uh.

07:47.633 --> 07:48.468
Uh...

07:49.594 --> 07:50.428
Well, uh...

07:50.928 --> 07:52.805
That blonde guy is Daichi Midorikawa!

07:52.889 --> 07:53.723
Huh?

07:53.806 --> 07:55.475
And the other guy's just a guy from some
other class!

07:55.558 --> 07:56.476
Introduce me right!

07:56.559 --> 07:57.393
HAHAHA

07:57.477 --> 07:58.311
Hayato Akahoshi!

08:00.813 --> 08:02.148
Yeah, yeah, I know.

08:02.231 --> 08:05.735
It's "aka" as in "Akahoshi," "hoshi" as
in "Akahoshi," together it's "Akahoshi"!

08:05.818 --> 08:07.320
Tone it down there, bro.

08:08.988 --> 08:11.407
ROOM 201 HIKAWA ROOM 401 AZUMI

08:11.491 --> 08:12.408
MIKI'S HOUSE

08:12.492 --> 08:14.035
Koyun, are you really not coming along

08:14.118 --> 08:16.537
- for the bike ride with us?
- I can't.

08:16.621 --> 08:17.872
I work tomorrow.

08:18.456 --> 08:19.290
Aw, man.

08:20.166 --> 08:23.169
I would just be in the way if I were
to come with them.

08:24.128 --> 08:25.379
It'll just be so cute, I'm dying

08:25.463 --> 08:26.756
to see it! Ooh!

08:34.305 --> 08:36.516
Yota is pretty cute, huh?

08:38.434 --> 08:39.685
What'd she say!?

08:40.186 --> 08:42.104
And so dependable and put together.

08:42.188 --> 08:43.272
IT'S THAT WAY

08:43.356 --> 08:44.941
You sure about that?

08:45.024 --> 08:45.942
THWACK

08:46.442 --> 08:49.904
I hope that one day, I could be as warm
and wonderful as Yota.

08:50.404 --> 08:51.739
Or even half as great.

08:52.323 --> 08:53.741
Huh? Ha!

08:53.824 --> 08:55.535
Wait, so what she's saying is, uh...

08:56.035 --> 08:58.663
Do you think Yota and Minato are that
different?

08:59.664 --> 09:01.290
Huh? What? Different how?

09:01.791 --> 09:03.876
Why'd she suddenly bring up Amamiya?

09:03.960 --> 09:07.255
Well, I mean obviously they're different
people, so of course-

09:07.755 --> 09:09.590
But that's not what you were asking.

09:10.424 --> 09:12.843
Why is she getting so flustered all of a
sudden?

09:14.303 --> 09:17.515
Around Amamiya though, I still get a
little nervous.

09:18.057 --> 09:19.850
Sometimes. Even now.

09:20.643 --> 09:23.229
Which means she doesn't get nervous
around Yota?

09:23.312 --> 09:26.440
MUTTER MUTTER

09:26.524 --> 09:30.111
I mean to be honest, I- I don't
know Amamiya as well as I know Yota yet.

09:30.194 --> 09:31.028
So, I just...

09:31.112 --> 09:33.197
I just feel like I wanna get to know him
better from now on.

09:33.281 --> 09:36.033
Wait, she said she prides herself on
knowing Yota well?!

09:36.117 --> 09:37.159
Gah!

09:44.875 --> 09:46.919
Mmm... Dam!

09:48.671 --> 09:50.423
HERE!

09:50.923 --> 09:52.800
Whoa, it's so cool!

09:53.926 --> 09:54.885
It is cool, huh?

09:54.969 --> 09:58.055
Yeah, super cool! It makes me all
tingly with excitement.

10:00.182 --> 10:02.059
Okay, Yota, get in the picture!

10:03.352 --> 10:04.186
Hm?

10:05.980 --> 10:06.814
Oh, no.

10:06.897 --> 10:07.898
What do I do?

10:08.399 --> 10:10.192
I can't fit the scenery in.

10:11.444 --> 10:12.278
Oh.

10:14.947 --> 10:17.241
THE WORD "ARM" DOESN'T
COME TO MIND EASILY

10:17.325 --> 10:19.285
- Here?
- Yeah, that's perfect.

10:19.368 --> 10:20.411
Yay!

10:23.205 --> 10:25.374
MEMORY OF DAM CURRY

10:30.713 --> 10:31.964
HAHA

10:32.048 --> 10:34.508
SOFT-SERVE ICE CREAM

10:47.480 --> 10:49.523
Ah! That was so much fun!

10:50.024 --> 10:51.150
It really was.

10:52.193 --> 10:53.861
- Yota.
- Huh?

10:53.944 --> 10:55.821
Where do you think we should go next?

10:56.947 --> 10:57.782
Oh.

10:57.865 --> 11:00.076
Wait, you told me you wanted to go to a
valley, right?

11:00.159 --> 11:01.786
Let's maybe go this summer!

11:12.046 --> 11:13.839
- Home!
- You're back!

11:13.923 --> 11:14.924
TRANSLATION: WELCOME BACK!

11:15.007 --> 11:16.300
So, how was your date?

11:17.093 --> 11:18.344
Date, yeah right.

11:18.427 --> 11:20.805
Things aren't like that between me
and Yota.

11:20.888 --> 11:22.890
Girls and guys can be friends, y'know.

11:22.973 --> 11:25.893
Ahhhh. That was just the best day ever!

11:25.976 --> 11:27.019
Must be nice.

11:27.520 --> 11:30.147
Well, I do wanna have a romantic
relationship one day.

11:30.231 --> 11:31.190
Don't get me wrong.

11:31.774 --> 11:33.109
But Yota is different.

11:33.192 --> 11:34.652
It's really not like that.

11:34.735 --> 11:36.195
I could never date him.

11:36.737 --> 11:38.656
- Really?
- Mm-hm.

11:39.156 --> 11:42.451
Besides that, friends are so much more
important than dating!

11:44.078 --> 11:45.871
- You're damn right.
- Right?

11:46.372 --> 11:49.333
- Brother and sister, we're the same.
- Brother and sister, we're the same.

11:49.417 --> 11:50.543
- Putting dating over friends is
- Putting dating over friends is

11:50.626 --> 11:51.836
- super lame!
- super lame!

11:51.919 --> 11:53.003
And that's my bro for ya!

11:53.087 --> 11:53.921
Ain't that right?

11:54.004 --> 11:55.673
- I know that's right.
- That's right.

11:55.756 --> 11:57.341
- Is that right?
- You know it's right!

11:57.425 --> 11:58.300
That's right!

12:09.812 --> 12:12.398
Oh, by the way, did you get that
freebie coupon for the crepe

12:12.481 --> 12:13.566
shop near the station?

12:13.649 --> 12:15.943
Huh?
I don't know what you're talking about.

12:16.026 --> 12:17.445
Then I need to send you the URL.

12:17.528 --> 12:19.864
You can only get like two per person, so
do it.

12:19.947 --> 12:20.990
Okay, thanks!

12:25.578 --> 12:26.829
Crepe URL!

12:34.378 --> 12:35.212
What?

12:36.255 --> 12:38.424
- You're not gonna take a picture first?
- Ahh.

12:38.507 --> 12:39.425
Uh.

12:39.925 --> 12:40.885
LET ME DOCUMENT IT...

12:40.968 --> 12:42.803
I guess it is pretty unique looking.

12:43.888 --> 12:45.014
Unique looking?

12:46.015 --> 12:47.892
- Oh, right.
- For some strange reason...

12:49.101 --> 12:52.438
I let Momoka somehow sway me into
taking a detour on the way home.

12:53.355 --> 12:56.233
I'll text it to you, so give me
your info, pretty please!

12:57.109 --> 12:57.943
Kay.

12:58.944 --> 13:01.655
Madame Koyun, I have a freebie coupon for
crepes.

13:01.739 --> 13:02.823
You wanna come with?

13:02.907 --> 13:04.742
Oh... Uh... Mm-hm.

13:05.451 --> 13:07.203
Why does she wanna go with me?

13:08.287 --> 13:09.413
Hey, so tell me your secret?

13:09.497 --> 13:12.583
What do I have to do to become
friends with guys like you have?

13:12.666 --> 13:13.793
They seem to flock to you.

13:13.876 --> 13:14.710
Huh?

13:15.586 --> 13:17.755
She thinks I'm some kind of
guy-whisperer?

13:17.838 --> 13:21.842
Honestly, I think you're way better with
people than I am, so I should be asking

13:21.926 --> 13:24.553
- you.
- Mm. Yeah, I guess, but y'know...

13:25.054 --> 13:26.430
She doesn't deny it.

13:26.931 --> 13:29.975
I could have the best people skills in
the world and I swear, I still couldn't

13:30.059 --> 13:31.977
get guys to treat me as a real friend.

13:32.728 --> 13:34.855
You do seem like you'd be popular with
guys.

13:34.939 --> 13:36.065
Oh, I am.

13:38.984 --> 13:40.820
You're thinking, "Wow. She's not
denying it."

13:40.903 --> 13:41.737
EEK

13:43.614 --> 13:45.324
You're so cute, Madam Koyun.

13:46.158 --> 13:49.787
I imagine this isn't the type of cute I
should be excited to be called.

13:49.870 --> 13:50.996
Oh.

13:51.080 --> 13:54.625
But sometimes, you think someone is
just nice as a friend, and then suddenly

13:54.708 --> 13:56.502
you've fallen for them.

13:57.127 --> 13:58.629
Has that ever happened to you?

13:59.129 --> 13:59.964
Huh?

14:01.173 --> 14:03.050
No, um, not really.

14:04.009 --> 14:06.887
Hm.
So you can completely separate the two.

14:06.971 --> 14:10.307
For some reason, I couldn't think for a
moment.

14:10.933 --> 14:11.767
Hm.

14:12.351 --> 14:14.144
That might be impossible for me.

14:15.187 --> 14:18.107
Because wouldn't you fall for him?

14:18.774 --> 14:19.900
Amamiya, I mean.

14:21.277 --> 14:24.655
If someone as handsome as him were
friends with me, well, I'd so end

14:24.738 --> 14:25.739
up falling for them.

14:27.032 --> 14:28.117
Handsome?

14:29.034 --> 14:30.661
Y- you think so?

14:31.912 --> 14:35.082
Why do I not have any issue or hesitation
complimenting Yota.

14:38.294 --> 14:40.588
But I struggle for words with Amamiya?

14:41.630 --> 14:43.299
GRADE 2 CLASS 2

14:43.799 --> 14:44.717
Thank you.

14:44.800 --> 14:45.759
The book was great.

14:46.635 --> 14:47.636
What? You read it?

14:48.137 --> 14:49.179
Yeah.

14:49.263 --> 14:50.764
I wanted to know what happened next.

14:50.848 --> 14:52.933
And to be able to talk about it with you.

14:53.684 --> 14:55.352
Wow. That's awesome.

14:58.105 --> 15:00.941
Oh no, Amamiya!
It's overflowing, tone it down!

15:01.025 --> 15:03.277
You're making your feelings too obvious.

15:03.819 --> 15:07.573
When that twist happened in the last
chapter, I literally got chills.

15:07.656 --> 15:09.408
Oh, I loved that part too-

15:14.038 --> 15:14.872
Huh?

15:15.664 --> 15:19.001
If someone as handsome as him were
friends with me, well, I'd so end

15:19.084 --> 15:20.085
up falling for them.

15:20.920 --> 15:23.047
No, it's not about him being handsome.

15:23.672 --> 15:27.051
It's the little things he says,
his actions, and expressions...

15:27.134 --> 15:28.385
They make me happy.

15:28.886 --> 15:30.930
My chest gets all tight, and I...

15:31.931 --> 15:33.641
Wait. Huh?

15:34.850 --> 15:35.976
I don't know why, but...

15:37.269 --> 15:39.438
She won't even look me in the eye today.

15:40.898 --> 15:43.651
What's up with her?
She seems kinda out of it.

15:44.360 --> 15:45.235
Is she okay?

15:46.070 --> 15:47.696
Hey, what book are you reading?

15:47.780 --> 15:48.614
THUMP

15:48.697 --> 15:49.531
Uh.

15:49.615 --> 15:52.242
I let Amamiya borrow it, and he's just
returned it.

15:52.326 --> 15:53.327
Wanna read it too?

15:53.827 --> 15:55.287
SHOCK...

15:55.371 --> 15:56.205
Huh?

15:56.872 --> 15:58.123
I read it in two days.

15:59.333 --> 16:01.085
I'm not trying to compete with you.

16:07.341 --> 16:08.175
Uh.

16:09.718 --> 16:10.552
Huh?

16:10.636 --> 16:11.470
FIDGETY

16:13.597 --> 16:16.892
Could this be just a one-sided,
unreciprocated thing from Amamiya?

16:16.976 --> 16:18.936
"Is not" instead of "does not" is used in
the negative sentence because the

16:19.019 --> 16:22.272
- subject is third-person singular...
- "What the heck am I feeling?"

16:24.149 --> 16:27.778
Yeah. I'm not so oblivious to my own
feelings that I'd start saying dumb

16:27.861 --> 16:29.196
things like that.

16:30.489 --> 16:31.323
Huh?

16:32.282 --> 16:33.117
What now?

16:34.076 --> 16:37.246
My feelings started changing before I
even realized it.

16:38.789 --> 16:39.707
- But...
- Hey, Koyun.

16:39.790 --> 16:40.624
Good morn-

16:41.417 --> 16:42.251
WHOOSH

16:42.334 --> 16:43.460
But that doesn't mean...

16:45.045 --> 16:46.797
That I'm gonna do anything about it

16:48.549 --> 16:50.259
Or that anything has to change.

16:55.973 --> 16:57.850
I'm spending my days how I always do.

16:58.475 --> 17:00.102
Uh. Huh?

17:01.645 --> 17:07.985
That said, I have to admit this giddy
feeling... is pretty fun.

17:10.070 --> 17:11.572
Alright, see you tomorrow.

17:11.655 --> 17:13.866
- Good practice today.
- Good practice today.

17:15.075 --> 17:15.951
- Oh?
- Hm?

17:16.035 --> 17:18.912
- You're not going to evening practice?
- Oh, there it is!

17:18.996 --> 17:20.122
Uh, yeah.

17:20.205 --> 17:22.958
I figured evening practice, it's mostly
people talking.

17:24.501 --> 17:27.796
So I thought it probably wouldn't be
a big deal if I wasn't there.

17:27.880 --> 17:28.714
Oh... I see.

17:29.381 --> 17:30.215
Koyuki!

17:30.716 --> 17:33.719
AFTER THE SPORTS FESTIVAL,
CHEER SQUAD COUPLES TEND TO FORM

17:33.802 --> 17:35.220
It's like built-in time to mingle
and get to know each other better!

17:35.304 --> 17:36.805
That's not a bad thing though!

17:36.889 --> 17:39.641
- Everyone knows that, that's why
- Oh, I've already memorized the

17:39.725 --> 17:42.227
- they come.
- choreography, so don't worry. I won't

17:42.311 --> 17:43.562
- fall behind.
- Don't blow this opportunity!

17:43.645 --> 17:44.480
See ya.

17:47.733 --> 17:49.526
Keep your chin up, Amamiya.

17:50.486 --> 17:52.404
EVENING PRACTICE

17:52.488 --> 17:54.656
PEOPLE ENGAGING IN SELF-PRACTICE TIME

17:54.740 --> 17:56.992
PEOPLE ENGAGING IN MINGLING TIME

17:58.285 --> 18:00.829
Did I say something wrong again?

18:02.581 --> 18:03.499
Oh, hey, Amamiya!

18:03.999 --> 18:05.042
Hm?

18:05.125 --> 18:06.418
Oh, thank goodness.

18:06.919 --> 18:08.295
I'm so relieved.

18:08.378 --> 18:09.421
Relieved?

18:10.047 --> 18:13.258
I was late, so I missed being able to
join up with the group.

18:14.218 --> 18:16.220
Can you maybe sit with me a bit?

18:20.307 --> 18:23.769
It seems like people are suddenly
getting closer with each other.

18:23.852 --> 18:25.020
Oh.

18:25.104 --> 18:26.271
That's definitely true.

18:27.356 --> 18:31.068
After the sports festival, I won't have a
chance to talk to you upperclassmen

18:31.151 --> 18:32.653
anymore, which makes me sad.

18:32.736 --> 18:33.737
Hm?

18:33.821 --> 18:35.364
You can keep talking to us after.

18:35.447 --> 18:36.490
What?

18:40.077 --> 18:40.911
Oh!

18:40.994 --> 18:43.872
I hung out with Madam Koyun the
other day, just the two of us.

18:43.956 --> 18:44.873
What?!

18:45.374 --> 18:47.668
Wait, when did they get all buddy-buddy?

18:48.502 --> 18:49.962
We ate crepes together.

18:51.004 --> 18:52.381
I took quite a few of us.

18:53.549 --> 18:54.383
Huh?

18:56.552 --> 18:59.388
Koyun's face! It's so hilarious!

19:02.307 --> 19:06.103
If she and I hung out again, would you
be cool with me inviting you next time?

19:06.186 --> 19:08.021
What? It'd be okay for me to join?

19:08.814 --> 19:09.648
Of course!

19:09.731 --> 19:12.234
Give me your info so I can message you
next time!

19:12.317 --> 19:14.153
Uh. Sure.

19:16.488 --> 19:19.116
You upperclassmen seem like you're all
really close.

19:20.159 --> 19:21.952
Madam Koyun told me about you guys.

19:22.452 --> 19:25.455
She told me about Miss Miki and about
Mister Yota too.

19:27.416 --> 19:28.250
Not me?

19:28.876 --> 19:31.712
I want the kind of relationship
Madam Koyun and Yota have.

19:31.795 --> 19:33.463
It seems very special.

19:34.298 --> 19:35.966
What kind of relationship?

19:36.049 --> 19:38.802
I don't know about you, but don't you
think the two of them should just

19:38.886 --> 19:39.720
date already?

19:39.803 --> 19:41.221
DOOM

19:42.222 --> 19:44.349
Because don't they look so cute together?

19:45.726 --> 19:47.227
Why would you say that?

19:47.311 --> 19:51.273
Well, we don't really know how the two
of them feel about each other.

19:51.982 --> 19:54.234
I know Yota still has a thing for Miki.

19:54.860 --> 19:57.196
I guess I don't know about Koyun though.

19:57.279 --> 19:58.530
Oh, that's true!

19:59.031 --> 19:59.990
I'm sorry.

20:00.073 --> 20:01.658
That was insensitive of me.

20:01.742 --> 20:03.160
Oh. No.

20:03.660 --> 20:07.539
Admittedly, I'd think that if you
found out that someone you thought of

20:07.623 --> 20:11.210
as just a friend actually liked you in
a different way than you did,

20:11.293 --> 20:14.880
and once you realized they look at you
in that way, it would feel a bit

20:14.963 --> 20:16.882
disgusting, wouldn't it?

20:16.965 --> 20:18.175
CRACK

20:18.258 --> 20:21.637
Depending on the situation, you might
even feel frightened by it.

20:22.179 --> 20:23.847
- Ugh.
- And also...

20:24.348 --> 20:25.641
There's more?

20:26.183 --> 20:29.603
Madam Koyun said the people she considers
friends would never become

20:29.686 --> 20:31.813
potential love interests.

20:33.148 --> 20:33.982
What?

20:40.447 --> 20:41.323
It makes me sick.

20:48.330 --> 20:50.832
Did I come on too strong?

22:23.550 --> 22:24.384
Aah!

22:26.887 --> 22:27.888
We made it!

22:32.726 --> 22:33.560
Ah!

22:37.939 --> 22:39.524
Wait, this is so awkward!

22:39.608 --> 22:41.860
I knew she was in our cheer squad, but...

22:41.943 --> 22:44.988
I gotta be honest, it's super
uncomfortable interacting with the

22:45.072 --> 22:47.949
sister of someone I had a full-on fight
with in the past.

22:48.450 --> 22:50.118
Atagawa, how's your sister doin'?

22:50.702 --> 22:51.536
- Huh?!
- Huh?

22:52.079 --> 22:53.622
What's goin' on with the face?

22:53.705 --> 22:55.916
You aren't curious how your ex
classmate is?

22:56.583 --> 22:57.876
Well, I mean...

22:58.752 --> 22:59.586
Huh?

23:00.629 --> 23:01.880
Do you really wanna know?

23:02.381 --> 23:03.256
EEK

23:05.175 --> 23:06.009
So many people!

23:10.305 --> 23:11.431
I'm really sorry.

23:11.932 --> 23:12.849
No.

23:12.933 --> 23:15.936
I- I'm sorry too
For taking up this door space.

23:18.563 --> 23:19.398
Koyuki?

23:20.065 --> 23:20.899
Hm?

23:20.982 --> 23:23.110
You're very close with Amamiya
aren't you?

23:24.236 --> 23:26.780
Huh? What does she mean by that?

23:27.280 --> 23:28.782
Yeah, I'd say we are.

23:29.282 --> 23:30.325
But then...

23:31.076 --> 23:33.995
In the soccer club, it's against
the rules for members and managers

23:34.079 --> 23:35.580
to get romantically involved.

23:37.749 --> 23:38.583
Momoka.

23:39.167 --> 23:42.754
You know how she's been hanging
around you a lot recently out of nowhere?

23:42.838 --> 23:45.006
Before that, she used to come around me.

23:46.007 --> 23:48.009
Do you realize what she wants?

23:50.887 --> 23:53.640
Could you please, maybe just
cheer her on?
